--------------------------------------------------------------------------

DATA

All data files in this repository and in its companion Hugging Face dataset —
the lexicon and corpus, prompts, held-out prompts, labels, word lists,
pre-registered predictions, extracted vectors, generations, coherence ladders and
atlases — are released under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
International (CC BY-SA 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/,
subject to the model notices below.

Why share-alike rather than CC BY. Sense glosses in the corpus derive in part
from Wiktionary, whose text is dual-licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 and GFDL; share-alike
requires material containing it to carry the same or a compatible licence. The
glosses are not confined to one file: every sense key has the form word::gloss,
so they appear in the labels, the predictions and the key list of every vector
file. Licensing all data CC BY-SA 4.0 is the simplest way to comply everywhere.

Attribution. Wiktionary content: https://www.wiktionary.org/ and its
contributors, used under CC BY-SA 4.0.

WordNet. Other glosses derive from Princeton WordNet 3.0, whose licence is
permissive and compatible with CC BY-SA, and requires this notice:

  WordNet Release 3.0 Copyright 2006 by Princeton University. All rights
  reserved. THIS SOFTWARE AND DATABASE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND PRINCETON
  UNIVERSITY MAKES NO REPRESENTATIONS OR WARRANTIES, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED.

LLM-assisted corpus. The LLM-judge filtering, the natural sentences and the
held-out prompts were produced with Devstral-Small-2-24B-Instruct-2512, run
locally; see that model's licence. The corpus cannot be regenerated exactly and
is released as fixed files, together with the prompts used to build it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

MODEL-DERIVED DATA

Model weights are not redistributed; models are referenced by Hugging Face
identifier. Three kinds of released file are nevertheless derived from the
models: extracted activation vectors, generated text, and atlases (which hold
int8 projections of each model's unembedding matrix). Each model's own licence
may apply to the files derived from it. As stated on the model cards at the time
of writing:

  google/gemma-3-1b-it, google/gemma-3-1b-pt,
  unsloth/gemma-2-9b-bnb-4bit            Gemma Terms of Use
  meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3-8B             Meta Llama 3 Community License.
                                         Built with Meta Llama 3.
  Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B                      Apache License 2.0
  mistralai/Mistral-7B-v0.3              Apache License 2.0
  EleutherAI/pythia-6.9b                 Apache License 2.0
  state-spaces/mamba-2.8b-hf             Apache License 2.0
  microsoft/phi-2                        MIT License

Users of the derived files are responsible for complying with the relevant
model licence; this notice is informational and not legal advice.

Generated text. Generations are model output produced under activation
steering, included so the analysis can be reproduced. Some are degenerate, and
some are emotionally charged by construction. They are research artifacts, not
endorsed content.

The NRC VAD Lexicon is not redistributed and no comparison against it is
included.
